tatement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n3\\text{det}(A)=3\\cdot 7=21.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n-2\\text{det}({A}^{T})=-2\\cdot 7=-14\\ne 14.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)+2\\text{det}(I)=7+2\\cdot 1=9.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139536163 true] [17592186386727 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386728 13194139536163 true] [17592186386727 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386729 13194139536163 true] [17592186386727 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386730 13194139536163 true] [17592186386727 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386731 13194139536163 true] [17592186386727 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386732 13194139536163 true] [17592186386727 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536163 true] [17592186386727 1041 "selection" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386727 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386729 13194139536163 true] [17592186386727 1110 #uuid "ee729036-e5b3-5f2a-8d4c-cffff53a5cef" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386728 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386728 1111 #uuid "0bb0c392-6f9b-50a1-b59e-3aa41d97d701" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386729 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386729 1111 #uuid "614b19c1-684c-574e-a7e0-53073b5de509" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386730 1034 "I only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386730 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386730 1111 #uuid "b99f49bb-c54e-5ac6-8893-08d43eabe20b" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386731 1034 "III only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386731 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386731 1111 #uuid "865d90ea-845d-5bbf-bfba-1a50652c7362" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386732 1034 "II only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386732 1111 #uuid "a885427a-47d7-583e-86e1-5bef313250f2" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386733 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386734 13194139536163 true] [17592186386733 1089 "q-130369" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386733 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536163 true] [17592186386733 1100 "Given that $det(A)=3$, which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $-4\\text{det}({A}^{T})+2\\text{det}(I)=3$\n- $2\\text{det}({A}^{T})=6$\n- $\\text{det}({A}^{T})-\\text{det}(I)=1$" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386733 1113 #uuid "5d5fee3b-3c65-5e23-9ab9-d1b7e28a665a" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386733 1145 "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\text{det}({A}^{T})=\\text{det}(A)=3\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ndet(I)=1.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n-4\\text{det}({A}^{T})+2\\text{det}(I)=-4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1=-10\\ne 3.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n2\\text{det}({A}^{T})=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\text{det}({A}^{T})-\\text{det}(I)=3-1=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386734 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386735 13194139536163 true] [17592186386734 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386736 13194139536163 true] [17592186386734 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386737 13194139536163 true] [17592186386734 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386738 13194139536163 true] [17592186386734 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386739 13194139536163 true] [17592186386734 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536163 true] [17592186386734 1041 "selection" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386734 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386739 13194139536163 true] [17592186386734 1110 #uuid "1c3bb8f0-1b40-5406-bc1e-8d1a35987f29" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386735 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386735 1111 #uuid "73de124a-ca7e-5d32-af90-623c434a4bfd" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386736 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386736 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386736 1111 #uuid "5aa26072-c8de-5ccd-bc63-2fdc3c9ac10c" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386737 1034 "I only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386737 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386737 1111 #uuid "cce77a39-b905-5954-903d-66d264362eba" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386738 1034 "None" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386738 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386738 1111 #uuid "d46c5514-677c-5029-84f1-c81c321d13e6" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386739 1034 "II only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386739 1111 #uuid "5bba5bcb-e382-5c9e-930c-199b8638fd5e" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386740 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386741 13194139536163 true] [17592186386740 1089 "q-158109" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386740 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536163 true] [17592186386740 1100 "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386740 1113 #uuid "899c253a-1c30-5e79-ad7a-1359c4288057" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386740 1145 "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]=(-3)\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=180.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|180|=180.\n$$" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386741 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386742 13194139536163 true] [17592186386741 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386743 13194139536163 true] [17592186386741 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386744 13194139536163 true] [17592186386741 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386745 13194139536163 true] [17592186386741 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386746 13194139536163 true] [17592186386741 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536163 true] [17592186386741 1041 "selection" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386741 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386742 13194139536163 true] [17592186386741 1110 #uuid "b4994727-d1aa-50b7-b14d-77cd23ffb5b3" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386742 1034 "180" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386742 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536163 true] [17592186386742 1111 #uuid "f3219801-1550-5a04-9a8b-71e331aa7536" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386743 1034 "140" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386743 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536163 true] [17592186386743 1111 #uuid "364092ba-8f9f-5190-823a-8ea199ff3eb6" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386744 1034 "240" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386744 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536163 true] [17592186386744 1111 #uuid "809b43d9-e397-564c-a186-49517cedd509" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386745 1034 "160" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386745 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536163 true] [17592186386745 1111 #uuid "c5ecd606-48c1-56c1-a33c-87703c3a370a" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386746 1034 "200" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536163 true] [17592186386746 1111 #uuid "222d9927-52c6-5088-ba88-b9b43049dc85" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386747 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386748 13194139536163 true] [17592186386747 1089 "q-158114" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386747 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536163 true] [17592186386747 1100 "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386747 1113 #uuid "fbc855b0-2fc8-59cd-b968-99ce98c10c34" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386747 1145 "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nNotice that the $2$nd row of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $3$rd row of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 3\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-6|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-6(4-25) \\\\  & =126.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|126|=126.\n$$" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386748 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386749 13194139536163 true] [17592186386748 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386750 13194139536163 true] [17592186386748 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386751 13194139536163 true] [17592186386748 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386752 1319413