 true] [17592186386754 1145 "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nNotice that the $1$st row of the determinant contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $2$nd row of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 4\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =8|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =8(-14+30) \\\\  & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|128|=128.\n$$" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386755 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386756 13194139536163 true] [17592186386755 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386757 13194139536163 true] [17592186386755 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386758 13194139536163 true] [17592186386755 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386759 13194139536163 true] [17592186386755 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386760 13194139536163 true] [17592186386755 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536163 true] [17592186386755 1041 "selection" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386755 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386758 13194139536163 true] [17592186386755 1110 #uuid "12c500df-95f4-50c2-aa02-f1eefe7a324c" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386756 1034 "64" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386756 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536163 true] [17592186386756 1111 #uuid "82f500b5-f6c3-5921-800b-061f948dc24c" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386757 1034 "16" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386757 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536163 true] [17592186386757 1111 #uuid "8b09dde9-89e4-54a1-b51b-42e5cf10e0e1" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386758 1034 "128" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386758 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536163 true] [17592186386758 1111 #uuid "16d238e0-10f6-5639-8101-2cab0584c7db" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386759 1034 "352" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386759 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536163 true] [17592186386759 1111 #uuid "174909cd-39c2-5a0b-a730-987442642a7f" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386760 1034 "176" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386760 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536163 true] [17592186386760 1111 #uuid "6a142f16-77ea-5813-b7d3-91a7ecfc8af6" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386761 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386762 13194139536163 true] [17592186386761 1089 "q-42876" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386761 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536163 true] [17592186386761 1100 "Given that $A=3I$, where $I$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $4\\text{det}({A}^{T})=108$\n- $\\text{det}(A)-6\\,\\text{det}(I)=0$\n- $\\text{det}({A}^{T})+\\text{det}(A)=54$" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386761 1113 #uuid "d586c1fa-f0c0-5b79-9eb6-60766e54ae95" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386761 1145 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3I & =3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a diagonal matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & ={3}^{3}=27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\text{det}({A}^{T})=\\text{det}(A)=27\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(I)=1.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n4\\text{det}({A}^{T})=4\\cdot 27=108\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-6\\,\\text{det}(I)=27-6\\cdot 1=21\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\text{det}({A}^{T})+\\text{det}(A)=27+27=54\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139536163 true] [17592186386762 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386763 13194139536163 true] [17592186386762 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386764 13194139536163 true] [17592186386762 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386765 13194139536163 true] [17592186386762 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386766 13194139536163 true] [17592186386762 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386767 13194139536163 true] [17592186386762 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536163 true] [17592186386762 1041 "selection" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386762 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386764 13194139536163 true] [17592186386762 1110 #uuid "f55b3ca9-578d-5df8-886a-69804198407f" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386763 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386763 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386763 1111 #uuid "b89c9ec2-77bf-5d55-ab02-93e10c88548f" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386764 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386764 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386764 1111 #uuid "9a677148-8b19-5ffb-9c45-725406c7f843" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386765 1034 "I only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386765 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386765 1111 #uuid "609f34aa-f176-5031-9466-976bb4864b3c" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386766 1034 "III only" 13194139536163 true] [17592186386766 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536163 true] [17592186386766 1111 #uuid "b7ec4a70-b328-55f0-bd8d-